.TH elfshaker-list-files 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-list\-files \- List files recorded in a snapshot.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker list\-files\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISNAPSHOT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists file metadata for a snapshot identified by its tag or as PACK:SNAPSHOT. Output lines are sorted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: %o %b %f]
Pretty\-print each result using placeholders:
	%o \- file checksum
	%f \- file name
	%h \- human\-readable size
	%b \- size in bytes
	%p \- permissions
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Use PATH as the data directory containing packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. This does not change the working directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISNAPSHOT\fR>
Snapshot tag or PACK:SNAPSHOT identifier to inspect.
